RetailCo Customer Segmentation Analysis

📌 Problem Statement
RetailCo operates multiple retail stores across different regions. Recently, management has noticed slowing customer growth and inconsistent repeat purchase behavior. They suspect that different customer groups have very different buying patterns, but they have never formally segmented their customer base.
They’ve shared with you their customer transaction data (Customer Segmentation dataset) and want you to:
1. Identify distinct customer segments.
2. Understand each segment’s behavior and value to the company.
3. Recommend targeted marketing actions to improve retention and sales


📊 Deliverables
- Excel-based segmentation analysis 
[Download the Excel Analysis](https://github.com/Sonali-Bera/Portfolio-Projects/blob/be5fc9c091be96d8363dcd396b3c374cf01c4bc1/excel/RetailCo_Customer_Segmentation_Analysis.xlsx)


💡 Marketing Actions
1. The highest revenue-earning segment is females aged 55–64 (21,000) and males aged 45–54 (18,850). 
   Despite contributing the most to revenue, these groups show low-to-medium purchase frequency, meaning their high spend is driven by fewer, larger transactions. - Introduce a premium loyalty program for older high-value customers (e.g., exclusive bundles, early access, personal shopping support).
2. Meanwhile, younger segments (18–34) contribute less revenue but purchase more frequently, indicating potential for long-term retention. - Introduce subscription models or repeat-purchase incentives (e.g., points system, cashback offers)
3. Monthly profits shows a positive upward trend, with female customers being the largest contributors to sustained growth.
4. Toys (sold in Australia and managed by Liam Brown) is the top-selling category, accounting for 22% of revenue; followed by clothing, groceries, furniture, and electronics.
 - For Toys (sold in Australia & female population being the highest purchaser group), could expand cross-sell opportunities (e.g., bundle toys with kids’ clothing or educational products, contribute a percentage of sales to a child-related cause, do family-focused marketing).
 - For Clothing (sold in South America & male segment dominating this space), promote seasonal collections, sportswear, workleisure and limited-time offers/drops.
 - For lagging categories like Electronics/Furniture, test bundled offers, influencer marketing or installment payment plans to boost adoption.


